In this specific example, the type annotations shown are equivalent, and you can use any of them as a shorthand for the others. However, in general, being specific about the values in your types is a good practice as it helps to prevent common mistakes, and can provide clearer intentions. So, while you could use `AutoAssertedTextType` in this case, being more specific about the possible values can be preferable. In this case, you could be more specific and write:

```type TextType = 10 | 'production-text';
```

